---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
import { COMPANY, PLANS, RELEASE, TRIAL, pageFor } from '../data/site';

// Only the memory app is listed (founder, session 79: coaching "is not a
// product", so its card is gone for now; the Knowledge Centre keeps it).
const page = pageFor('/products/');
---
<Base page={page}>
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Products</h1>
    <p>Zaaheen is a {COMPANY.city} company that builds software for people who use AI every day.
       Our first product gives your AI apps a private memory that stays on your own computer.</p>

    <div class="cards">
      <a class="card" href="/">
        <div class="card-brand"><Logo size={40} /><h2>Zaaheen</h2></div>
        <p>A private memory for your AI assistants. Your AI apps share one memory about you,
           stored and encrypted on your own computer.</p>
        <span class="card-link">See the memory app</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2>What the memory app does</h2>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>One memory for all your AI apps.</strong> Tell Claude something once, and Cursor or
          ChatGPT can recall it. <a href="/docs/#connecting">How to connect your AI apps</a></li>
      <li><strong>It stays on your computer.</strong> Your memories are stored and encrypted on your
          device, and never uploaded. <a href="/ai-and-your-data/">What we can and can't see</a></li>
      <li><strong>You stay in charge.</strong> See every memory, forget any one, download them all, or
          delete everything in one step. <a href="/docs/#memories">Looking after your memories</a></li>
      <li><strong>For Windows and Mac.</strong> {RELEASE.windows.arch} {RELEASE.windows.tested}, or a Mac
          with an Apple chip (M1 or newer). {TRIAL.days} days free, then {PLANS.monthly} or
          {PLANS.yearly}. <a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
